@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+# Toolbar backing during asynchronous navigation
+
+ReaderInkView paints a live surface snapshot while asynchronous navigation is
+in progress, then its stationary toolbar and floating controls. Toolbar button
+cells and their enclosing frame are transparent: ordinary editor rendering
+provides their opaque backing through the surrounding canvas bands.
+
+The live path must restore that backing after the snapshot and before painting
+tool marks, buttons, icons and dark-theme inversion. Otherwise page pixels show
+between the icons only during navigation. It now clears the toolbar rectangle
+to white before those existing paint steps. Dark mode then inverts the finished
+bar as usual. A hidden toolbar paints no rectangle.
+
+Only the toolbar is cleared. The old editable area's bounds can reflect the
+source panel's crop, while the live camera has already moved; clearing all its
+surrounding bands could obscure valid animation pixels. No provider identities,
+document-coordinate mappings or annotation data changes are involved.
+
+`tests/realbb/surface_toolbar.lua` checks actual blitter pixels through the real
+ReaderInkView paint/layout/theme paths. Host widgets/input and the generic book
+are fixtures; buttons are represented by small opaque icon tiles in transparent
+cells. The original code fails 48 toolbar comparisons in a 112-check run. The
+expanded final suite passes 160 checks across all four toolbar sides, light/dark,
+grayscale/color, repeated live frames, hidden toolbars and a stale canvas clip.
+
+Run from a built KOReader runtime:
+
+```
+./luajit REPO/tests/realbb/surface_toolbar.lua REPO
+```
+
+It is registered in the native test runner. Physical refresh behavior and actual
+SVG rendering/input remain separate live checks.
